  "answer": "The KX-100 cannot do this measurement, for two independent reasons. First, its frequency range is 10 MHz to 18 GHz, so a 40 GHz signal is outside the band: SENS:FREQ refuses 40 GHz with error -222 and no calibrated reading is possible at that frequency. Second, its measurement resolution is fixed at 0.01 dB, so 0.001 dB readings are not available; averaging reduces noise but does not extend the resolution. The manual states explicitly that no setting or averaging count extends these limits. You will need a power sensor rated to at least 40 GHz with 0.001 dB display resolution; the KX-100 on the bench is not suitable for this qualification.",
